// Internal world, lighting, and encounter launch definitions.
//
// A scenario is a world plus the units standing on it. Campaign, Sandbox, saves,
// retries, review, and tests resolve these records; there is no player-facing browser.
// `default_game` names the canonical scenario bound by a new Campaign.
//
// Order is the order they are listed, so it is your decision rather than an accident.
//
// FIELDS
//
//   name      stable internal launch identity
//   category  REQUIRED inert compatibility metadata. Runtime routing ignores it.
//   blurb     descriptive compatibility text retained for internal/review inputs
//   world     the map file, as a path under `assets/`
//   lighting  OPTIONAL sun/sky/cloud file. Omit it for the shipped look
//   generation_seed  OPTIONAL Some(reproducible seed) for generated maps
//   starting_time_hours  OPTIONAL Some(hour in [0, 24)) for cyclic lighting
//   encounter who is on the map and where they start, as a path under `assets/`
//
// `lighting` is what makes one scenario feel unlike another as much as its terrain
// does -- it carries the sun's angle and colour, so it decides which way the shadows
// fall, not just what the sky looks like.
//
// The `world`, `lighting` and `encounter` paths are NOT checked by the compiler —
// nothing here knows what a map is, deliberately, so that this file does not have to be
// edited whenever the map format changes. A typo is caught by tests that open every file
// named here, so a wrong path fails `cargo test` rather than at the loading screen.
//
// An `encounter` is a roster: many units a side, each naming an archetype and a
// placement. Several generated maps share the anchored skirmish, while non-combat
// traversal and biome reviews may reuse one standard showcase party. The placement
// vocabulary and how to add a party member are documented in the encounter files.
//
// Authored maps place units on exact CUBE coordinates; generated maps use the named
// anchors the generator publishes after validating the map, so rerolling a seed does not
// require rewriting coordinates. Either way, a unit that cannot be placed returns to the
// Main Menu with the reason — it never silently moves to the centre of the map.
(
    default_game: "Party Trial",
    scenarios: [
        (
            name: "The Crossing",
            category: Map,
            blurb: "A river with one bridge over it, a mountain, and a switchback up the side.",
